id: E260
trigger_tool: conan|meson|gnome|pkg-config|shadow-ci
phase: packaging|build|testing|verification
error_signature: meson_three_part_version|meson_gnome_tools_missing|glib_mkenums|glib_genmarshal|g_libintl_symbols|usr_bin_env_unusable|so_symlink_missing|ohos_elf_signing

severity: 3
category: ohos-gnome-meson-glib-consumer
match_keywords: atk,GNOME,Meson,glib,gobject,glib-mkenums,glib-genmarshal,g_libintl,libintl,host_machine.system,harmonyos,introspection,shared library symlink,binary-sign-tool
title: GNOME/Meson GLib consumer packages on OHOS need Meson option/version review, pkg-config tool variables, Python wrappers, libintl link args, library aliases, and installed ELF signing

root_cause: |
  GNOME Meson libraries that consume GLib/GObject often rely on pkg-config variables such
  as glib_mkenums and glib_genmarshal, assume GLib helper scripts can execute through
  /usr/bin/env, and use Linux-only Meson host checks for linker flags. On OHOS, Meson
  reports host_machine.system() as harmonyos, /usr/bin/env may be unavailable in the
  runner environment, shared-library symlink creation can be unreliable, and installed
  ELF shared libraries may need re-signing before runtime tests can execute. Older GNOME
  Meson files also require option and version review; ATK 2.28.0 declares project version
  2.28 while later code reads version[2], so the recipe carries a small source patch to
  use 2.28.0.
affected_scope: ATK 2.28.0.1 and similar GNOME Meson libraries that consume GLib/GObject on OHOS

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: |
  For small GNOME Meson GLib consumers:
  (1) Inspect meson_options.txt for the exact option names; older releases may use
      disable_introspection=true and enable_docs=false instead of newer introspection/docs
      option names.
  (2) Patch incomplete Meson project versions when upstream reads major/minor/micro from
      meson.project_version().split('.').
  (3) Use PkgConfigDeps and MesonToolchain with wrap_mode=nodownload and default_library.
  (4) Augment generated glib-2.0.pc and gobject-2.0.pc with glib_mkenums,
      glib_genmarshal, and related variables if Meson's GNOME module expects them.
  (5) If GLib helper scripts use an unreliable /usr/bin/env shebang on the tested OHOS
      device, create small Python wrappers that run the dependency package's helper scripts
      with sys.executable.
  (6) Treat Meson host_machine.system() == 'linux' checks as portability review points;
      extend to ['linux', 'harmonyos'] only for Linux-compatible flags that are valid on OHOS.
  (7) Prefer recipe-side link args to the GLib package's libintl.so/libintl.a for g_libintl_*
      resolution before adding package-specific source wrapper files.
  (8) Create libfoo.so and soname aliases after build/package when symlink creation is
      unavailable; copy as fallback.
  (9) Re-sign installed OHOS ELF shared libraries during package().
  (10) Keep upstream Meson tests enabled and run meson.test() when can_run() is true; add a
       non-empty C/CMake test_package that includes public headers and resolves runtime types
       or functions.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: gnome-meson-glib-consumer-pattern

forbid_1_pattern: applying_newer_meson_option_names_without_checking_meson_options
forbid_1_reason: older GNOME releases can use disable_introspection/enable_docs instead of introspection/docs
forbid_1_consequence: meson setup fails with unknown options
forbid_2_pattern: adding_intl_wrapper_source_before_linking_glib_libintl
forbid_2_reason: recipe-side libintl link args can solve g_libintl_* with less upstream patch surface
forbid_2_consequence: unnecessary source patch and harder review
forbid_3_pattern: test_package_without_public_api_call|empty_smoke_test
forbid_3_reason: library test_package must prove headers, exported symbols, and runtime loader path
forbid_3_consequence: L1 negative test may fail or test quality is weak

